{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>When He enlarges.</b> This passage was already stated above, and He returned and repeated it because it is said in it, below, 'and you shall make your burnt-offerings.' Another interpretation: because everything written in it is recurrent every day, and He returned and repeated them so that they would be accustomed and expert in it." "<b>As He has spoken to you.</b> And where did He speak? 'And you shall broaden your border,' etc." "<b>And you shall say: I will eat meat.</b> From here that a person should not buy a litra of meat unless he has first deliberated." "<b>When your soul desires.</b> 'כי' in place of 'אם' (if)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:36.284975485Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}